From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Maago <maago@example.com>
Date: Mon, 5 Oct 2026 02:25:55 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Comments, and hide what has them

Comment on a post. Deleting a post hides it.

- The comment form is CommentForm (model=Comment). The post page draws
  the post, its comments and the form on GET; a POST to the same path
  adds a comment. Two routes, post_detail and comment_create, and two
  views on one In:

      func ShowPost(ctx context.Context, db maago.DB, in ShowPostIn) (PostPage, error)
      func CreateComment(ctx context.Context, tx maago.Tx, in ShowPostIn) (maago.Result[PostPage], error)

  Both build the page with one helper, postPage(ctx, db, id, f): GET
  passes its db, POST its tx, a maago.DB too. A form that does not pass
  shows the same page again, with its errors
- A comment points at its post (fk=Post). DELETE a post with comments
  and the database refuses. So deleting hides the post instead: it turns
  Post.Hidden on, in HidePost, the view of POST /posts/{id}/delete
  (post_delete), with its tx. Its comments go out of sight with it, and
  stay in the database
- Hidden bool default=false. maago makemigrations --name hide_posts
  writes 0002. maago gen stops at recent_posts.sql again: select the new
  column
- Every query gets NOT p.hidden: the list, the search, one post, and the
  pinned overlap. The page of a hidden post is a 404, as PostDetail
  finds no row, and no comment can go on it
- The same-title check (post_title_taken.sql) counts hidden posts too:
  the model's unique=(BoardID,Title) holds for them as well

Deleting a hidden post for real comes later, with asking whether who
deletes it wrote it.

